# Toyota Corolla E110 five-door liftback, 1997-2002.
#
# The eighth-generation Corolla. UK launch 23 June 1997; a revised range
# followed on 1 February 2000, which deleted the saloon because it took half a
# per cent of British Corolla sales; replaced in January 2002 when the E120
# went on sale on 2 January 2002.
# https://mag.toyota.co.uk/toyota-corolla-generations-1997-2001/
# https://media.toyota.co.uk/new-corolla-in-the-uk-market/
#
# Dimensions 4.270 x 1.690 x 1.380 m, wheelbase 2.465 m. Source: English
# Wikipedia, "Toyota Corolla (E110)" infobox: wheelbase 2,465 mm (Randall 2006,
# p. 247); liftback length 4,270 mm (hatchback 4,120 mm, sedan 4,315 mm); width
# 1,690 mm; height 1,380 mm for hatchback, liftback and sedan. The fitted model
# measures 4.2705 m, 5.5 mm over target, 1.690 m wide, with the wheel centres
# 2.465 m apart (57.7 per cent of length). Mirrors extend beyond the hull.
#
# Shape reference: the pack's image 1 is a shallow front-left three-quarter,
# not a level elevation (the larger near-side front wheel is perspective), so
# the model was compared at that actual angle and a separate true elevation was
# rendered for coherence. Image 1 supplied the five-door profile, glazing and
# arches; image 2 the front lamps, grille and intakes; image 3 the liftback
# hatch and tail; image 4 the far-side rear lamp cluster. No boot is modelled.
# The British car was the five-door liftback, which Toyota expected to be the
# largest-selling body.
#
# Colours are Toyota GB brochure names, evidence grade (a): the MY1999 brochure
# (Edition Two, December 1998) lists Pure White, Cool Water, Solar Red, Steel
# Blue, British Green, Lucerne Silver, Aubergine, Satin Black, Night Shadow and
# Sunburst Red. Four common British finishes are modelled: Lucerne Silver, Pure
# White, Satin Black and Solar Red. Weights silver 3, white 3, red 2, black 2,
# total 10, provisional pending the central rebase.
#
# Speed 180 km/h, the 1.6-litre car's quoted maximum. Comfort 85/310, on the
# line 180 + 1.5 x 85: a quiet, well-finished family hatchback, a step above
# the E100. Classes 1,2.
#
# Dates are road presence: June 1997 intro, retires staggered 2010-2013 on a
# thirteen- to sixteen-year tail.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/toyota-corolla-e110.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/toyota-corolla-e110.dae (65 objects). References:
# citycars/references/toyota-corolla-e110/ (gitignored; Wikimedia Commons).
#
# Accepted deviations: the nose is more rounded and bulbous than the
# photographs and the headlamp reflectors read as separate discs rather than
# elements behind a common lens; the rear quarter glass is too pointed, the
# hatch glass too rectangular and the rear lamp clusters too round; the wheel
# arches show abrupt shading transitions. The top view and raised turn confirm
# a continuous body-coloured roof. At 128 px the rounded liftback profile and
# the steep hatch read as the eighth-generation Corolla.

obj=citycar
name=ToyotaCorollaE110(LucerneSilver)
copyright=JamesPetts

DistributionWeight=3
intro_year=1997
intro_month=6
retire_year=2013
retire_month=6
speed=180
class=1,2
maximum_comfortable_journey_minutes=85
maximum_tolerable_journey_minutes=310

